      ":question/problem": "Consider the equation in the variable $x,$ given by\n\n$$\n-6(q-8)x=-3\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ax=b.$ In this case,\n\n$$\na=-6(q-8),\\,b=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n-6(q-8)=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6(q-8) &=0 \\\\ \\frac{-6(q-8)}{-6} &=\\frac{0}{-6} \\\\ q-8 &=0 \\\\ q &=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
